<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Spanish Bougie</h1><p class="st-meta">1510 CE – 1555 CE · capital Bejaia</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Bejaia under Spanish occupation, a contested fortress that resisted the Barbarossa brothers for decades before falling to Ottoman Algiers.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In January 1510 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-navarro">Pedro Navarro</a> captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bejaia">Bejaia</a>, then ruled by a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hafsid-dynasty">Hafsid</a> prince, as part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain's</a> campaign along the North African coast after the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a>. The conquest made Bejaia a Spanish presidio comparable to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/spanish-oran">Spanish Oran</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Spanish held only the town and its forts, with a garrison cut off from the hinterland, where the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-kuku">Kingdom of Kuku</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-ait-abbas">Kingdom of Ait Abbas</a> held sway. The corsair <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oruc-reis">Oruç Barbarossa</a> attacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bejaia">Bejaia</a> in 1512 and 1514 and lost his arm in the first attempt. The port's trade declined sharply.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1555 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salah-rais">Salah Rais</a>, beylerbey of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/regency-of-algiers">Regency of Algiers</a>, besieged and took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bejaia">Bejaia</a>. Its governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alonso-de-peralta">Alonso de Peralta</a> surrendered and was executed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> for doing so. The city became part of Ottoman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="colony, 1510 CE – 1555 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 64 H80 L70 78 H30 Z"/><path d="M50 64 V18"/><path d="M50 22 L72 56 H50"/><path d="M50 28 L32 56 H50"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">colony</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:89.75%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1510 CE – 1555 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Bejaia</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Alonso de Peralta</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Spanish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/algeria">Algeria</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Spanish Bejaia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1532&amp;focus=spanish-bougie" aria-label="Spanish Bougie on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4807 853 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Spanish Bougie lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5127 1109L4910 989M5127 1109L5077 1108"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4910 989h0M5077 1108h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5127 1109h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5127 1109h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Bejaia. <a href="/atlas?year=1532&amp;focus=spanish-bougie">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

